<div class="bt">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim, Volume 2</div>
<div class="ht">Hilchos Tefilas Arvis [Laws of the Evening Prayer]<br>Halachos 1–3</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!--                     HALACHAH 1 (on LM I:60)                  -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->

<div class="ts">
<div class="sn">Halachah 1</div>
<div class="ssn">Tefilas Arvis Reshus, v'ha'idana kav'uha alaihu chovah<br>[The evening prayer is optional, but nowadays they have established it upon themselves as an obligation]</div>
</div>

<div class="p">Based on what Rabbainu wrote in the teaching <span class="v">"Pasach R' Shimon"</span> (<span class="lr">LM I:60</span>): that through <span class="h">yirah</span> [fear/awe of Hashem] one merits great wealth, and through this wealth one comes to <span class="h">hisbonenus</span> [deep contemplation] of the Torah. For through <span class="h">yirah</span> one subdues the aspect of <span class="v">"charm is false and beauty is vain"</span> — see there well.</div>

<div class="p">Now, Yaakov is the aspect of <span class="h">yirah</span>, as the Zohar states: <span class="v">"b'yirasecha"</span> [in Your awe] — in the merit of Yaakov, who said <span class="v">"how awesome [<i>nora</i>]."</span> Therefore he was not afraid at all of the aspect of <span class="v">"vain beauty."</span> Therefore we do not find regarding Yaakov that his marital union was ever forbidden to him, even when he descended to Egypt — on the contrary, Hashem assured him: <span class="v">"I will go down with you to Egypt, and I will also surely bring you up"</span> etc. For Yaakov's bed was complete, and he guarded the <span class="h">Bris</span> exceedingly, and he had no hold or fear from the aspect of <span class="v">"vain beauty."</span> All this was because he merited the aspect of <span class="h">yirah</span>, which subdues the aspect of <span class="v">"vain beauty"</span> as mentioned above. On account of this, Yaakov merited exceedingly great wealth, as it is written: <span class="v">"and you shall spread out to the west and to the east"</span> etc. — meaning an inheritance without boundaries, meaning the aspect of all the wealth of the world. For all the <span class="h">Avos</span> merited great wealth according to their level of <span class="h">yirah</span>, according to how much they subdued <span class="v">"vain beauty."</span> But Yaakov, who was the perfection of <span class="h">yirah</span> and merited to subdue entirely the aspect of <span class="v">"vain beauty"</span> as mentioned above — therefore he merited the ultimate wealth, meaning all the wealth of the world, an inheritance without boundaries as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span> is <span class="h">reshus</span> [optional]. For <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span> is the aspect of Yaakov, for he established it, and he is the aspect of <span class="h">yirah</span> as mentioned above, through which one merits great wealth, through which one merits the great <span class="h">hisbonenus</span> mentioned above. Therefore it is <span class="h">reshus</span>, for when one merits this <span class="h">hisbonenus</span>, then there is no obligation to pray. For this <span class="h">hisbonenus</span> is the aspect of the attainment of R' Shimon bar Yochai, who merited this. Therefore he was exempt from prayer, as our Sages of blessed memory said. For this <span class="h">hisbonenus</span> is the aspect of <span class="mx">"his Torah is his craft"</span> — meaning that all his craft and wealth is solely from the Torah, the aspect of the chips of the Tablets from which Moshe became wealthy, as our Master, our Teacher and our Rebbe wrote there — see there. And this is what our Sages of blessed memory said: <span class="mx">"they only taught [the exemption from prayer] regarding someone like R' Shimon bar Yochai and his colleagues, whose Torah is their craft"</span> etc. According to the simple meaning this is puzzling, for are there not also now people who have no craft at all and only engage in Torah — how much more so in the days of the Shas! But the essential thing depends on the <span class="h">hisbonenus</span> mentioned above, which depends on wealth. Therefore it is called <span class="mx">"their Torah is their craft"</span> as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore Yaakov specifically established <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span>. For then, at night, the time is more conducive to attainments and <span class="h">hisbonenus</span>, as it is written in the Shivchei HaBa'al Shem Tov that most Torah <span class="h">chiddushim</span> are merited at night. And as Rabbainu wrote (<span class="lr">LM I:52</span>) that at night it is more conducive to <span class="h">bitul</span> [self-nullification] — see there. Also, the night is the aspect of wealth, the aspect of <span class="v">"she tasted that her commerce is good; her lamp does not go out at night."</span> For wealth comes from there, as is implied in several places in the words of Rabbainu — for one who examines there. Therefore <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span> is <span class="h">reshus</span> as mentioned above. But nowadays they have established it upon themselves as an obligation. For now, one does not merit this level of attainment even at night, and therefore it is an obligation to pray as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore in the evening one recites two <span class="h">berachos</span> before <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> and two after it. But in the morning one recites only three <span class="h">berachos</span> — two before it and one after it. For <span class="h">Arvis</span>, which corresponds to Yaakov who merited an inheritance without boundaries — the aspect of <span class="v">"and you shall spread out to the west and to the east, to the north and to the south"</span> — and corresponding to this one recites four <span class="h">berachos</span> before and after <span class="h">Krias Shma</span>, corresponding to the four directions of the world. For one merits then the inheritance of Yaakov, an inheritance without boundaries. But at <span class="h">Shacharis</span> one recites only three <span class="h">berachos</span>, corresponding to three directions of the world's structure, for the north is lacking. There, the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> overpowers — the aspect of <span class="v">"from the north evil shall break forth"</span> etc. For <span class="h">Shacharis</span> corresponds to Avraham, who in his days had not yet entirely subdued the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> and had not yet merited an inheritance without boundaries. But Yaakov merited to subdue it entirely and merited to conquer all four directions of the world, even the northern direction. Since he subdued the northern direction, therefore he merited great wealth whose essence comes from there — the aspect of <span class="v">"from the north gold shall come."</span> Therefore they added a fourth <span class="h">berachah</span> at <span class="h">Arvis</span>, which was established corresponding to the aspect of Yaakov as mentioned above — and this is the <span class="h">berachah</span> of <span class="h">Hashkiveinu</span>. Therefore we then request: <span class="v">"spread over us the shelter of Your peace"</span> — this is the aspect of Yaakov, the aspect of <span class="v">"Yaakov journeyed to Sukkos."</span> And this is why we then request regarding the awakening of sleep, as we say: <span class="v">"stand us up, our King"</span> etc. — for through this one merits the aspect of <span class="h">yirah</span>, as explained there in the words of Rabbainu — see there well. And this is: <span class="v">"and establish us with good counsel from before You"</span> — for through the awakening of sleep the power of speech comes to the organs of procreation, which are the kidneys that counsel. See there well.</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!--                     HALACHAH 2 (on LM I:19)                  -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->

<div class="ts">
<div class="sn">Halachah 2</div>
<div class="ssn">The matter of three prayers per day — meaning two by day and one at night</div>
</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> [the Holy Tongue] through <span class="h">Lashon Targum</span> [the Aramaic language], which is the aspect of <span class="h">shnayim mikra v'echad targum</span> [reading the Torah portion twice and the Targum once], as explained in the teaching <span class="v">"Tefilah l'Chavakuk"</span> (<span class="lr">LM I:19</span>).</div>

<div class="p">For prayer is the aspect of <span class="h">Malchus</span> as is known, the aspect of Chavah-Woman, the aspect of the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span>. Therefore one prays two prayers by day and one at night, in the aspect of <span class="h">shnayim mikra v'echad targum</span> as mentioned above. For <span class="h">shnayim mikra</span> is the aspect of the Written Torah, which is the aspect of day, as brought in the words of Rabbainu of blessed memory (there, Siman 3), and corresponding to this one prays two prayers by day. And <span class="h">echad targum</span> is the aspect of night, which is the aspect of sleep and deep slumber, the aspect of <span class="h">Targum</span>, as explained well in the teaching mentioned above — and this is the aspect of the Oral Torah. For the <span class="h">Targum</span> is the explanation of the Torah, and it is included in the Oral Torah; also, most of the Oral Torah — meaning the Talmud — was composed in the language of <span class="h">Targum</span>. For <span class="h">Targum</span> is the aspect of the Oral Torah, which is the aspect of night, as Rabbainu of blessed memory wrote (there). Therefore one prays one prayer at night, corresponding to the aspect of <span class="h">echad targum</span>, which is the aspect of night as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore Yaakov established <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span>. For the essential building of the aspect of Chavah-Woman is through deep slumber — meaning the essential building and perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> is specifically through <span class="h">Lashon Targum</span>, as explained there. And Yaakov merited this — meaning he merited the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> through the <span class="h">Targum</span>: meaning through fighting and subduing the hold of evil within the <span class="h">Targum</span> — which is the aspect of the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil — and he clarified the good from there, and through this he merited the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span>. Therefore Yaakov is the choicest of the <span class="h">Avos</span> and his bed was complete without any flaw. This is the aspect of the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span>, which is the aspect of a complete bed, the aspect of guarding the <span class="h">Bris</span> in perfection — which one merits through the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> through the <span class="h">Targum</span>, as explained there. As it is written regarding Yaakov that he said: <span class="v">"my strength and the beginning of my vigor"</span> — meaning guarding the <span class="h">Bris</span>, which one merits through this as mentioned above. Therefore he merited to establish the twelve <span class="h">Shevatim</span>, which are the aspect of the twelve oxen upon which the holy <span class="h">Malchus</span> stands — meaning the aspect of the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span>, the aspect of guarding the <span class="h">Bris</span>.</div>

<div class="p">And this is the aspect of the seventy souls that came forth from Yaakov — he merited this through the aspect of the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span>. For through this one subdues the all-encompassing evil of the seventy nations. Therefore he merited to establish seventy souls of the house of Yaakov. All this is essential through <span class="h">Lashon Targum</span>, which is the aspect of the Tree of Knowledge, for Yaakov was engaged in repairing and clarifying the Tree of Knowledge — repairing the flaw of Adam HaRishon, as is known. For the seventy souls of the house of Yaakov, and conversely the seventy nations, all hold onto the aspect of the root-hold of the Tree of Knowledge — where the aspect of Yaakov resides, as brought in the Writings [of the Ari"zal]. Therefore the essential wars of Yaakov were with his father-in-law Lavan the Aramean. For Lavan the Aramean is the aspect of <span class="h">Targum</span>, which is the Aramaic language, and as Rabbainu of blessed memory wrote in the teaching mentioned above: Lavan called it <span class="v">"Yegar Sahadusa"</span> in order to draw and nurse from holiness through <span class="h">Lashon Targum</span>. And Yaakov called it <span class="v">"Gal'ed"</span> in order to complete <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> — see there.</div>

<div class="p">It emerges that Yaakov, whose essential task was to repair the Tree of Knowledge, was therefore engaged in subduing the aspect of Lavan the Aramean — meaning subduing the evil within the <span class="h">Targum</span> and raising the good, to build the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> — the aspect of Chavah-Woman — through this specifically, as mentioned above. Therefore Yaakov took his wives specifically from the daughters of Lavan — meaning he merited the aspect of Chavah-Woman, which is the aspect of Leah and Rachel, through the <span class="h">Targum</span> which is the aspect of Lavan, as mentioned above. Meaning he subdued the evil and extracted the good, and through this specifically the aspect of the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> was built — the aspect of Chavah-Woman, the aspect of Leah and Rachel. Therefore Yaakov merited the ultimate perfection and his bed was complete, and he established twelve <span class="h">Shevatim</span> and seventy souls. For he merited to subdue the evil within the <span class="h">Targum</span> and to clarify the good, until he merited the aspect of the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> through <span class="h">Targum</span> specifically — meaning he merited to take Leah and Rachel from the house of Lavan specifically, who is the aspect of <span class="h">Targum</span> as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">And this is what Yaakov sent to Esav: <span class="v">"I dwelt with Lavan"</span> etc. For Yaakov fled from Esav to Lavan — meaning Yaakov knew that it is impossible to subdue Esav, who is the filth of the Serpent, the all-encompassing evil, except by cutting off his nourishment — meaning by subduing the evil within the <span class="h">Targum</span> from where they nurse, and raising the good to <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span>. Then Esav, who is the aspect of all-encompassing evil, will automatically fall and be nullified, as explained there in the teaching mentioned above. Therefore Yaakov fled specifically to Lavan, in order to repair <span class="h">Lashon Targum</span>, and then Esav would fall automatically as mentioned above. And he merited to triumph over him and extracted from there specifically the aspect of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> — meaning Chavah-Woman as mentioned above. Therefore he said <span class="v">"I will serve you seven years"</span> — corresponding to the aspect of the seventy nations that are included in seven, whose nourishment is from the aspect of Lavan, from the aspect of <span class="h">Targum</span> as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore he had to serve him specifically those seven years. For when one desires to clarify the good from within the evil, one must pass through there and endure their exile and servitude, and stand firm in the test to break them and subdue them — and then specifically one clarifies the good from there. Therefore after the exile of those seven years — which is the aspect of the exile of the seventy nations as mentioned above — then he merited the aspect of the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span>, which is the aspect of Rachel and Leah as mentioned above. Therefore he was waiting until Yosef was born, who is the aspect of tikun of the <span class="h">Bris</span>. And then, when Rachel gave birth to Yosef, his <span class="h">da'as</span> was strengthened and he understood that he had merited the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> through <span class="h">Targum</span>, until he merited through this Yosef — meaning guarding the <span class="h">Bris</span>. Therefore he said then: <span class="v">"send me away"</span> etc. And our Sages of blessed memory said that he was no longer afraid of Esav since Yosef was born, who is his adversary etc. For certainly he has nothing to fear now, since he merited to establish Yosef through Rachel the daughter of Lavan the Aramean. This is the aspect of guarding the <span class="h">Bris</span> through meriting <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span>, which one builds through <span class="h">Targum</span> specifically, as mentioned above. And this is what is written: <span class="v">"when Rachel gave birth to Yosef"</span> — <span class="v">"Rachel"</span> specifically, who is the aspect of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> and she is the daughter of Lavan. For her building is from the <span class="h">Targum</span> as mentioned above. And through this specifically Yosef was born — the aspect of guarding the <span class="h">Bris</span> as mentioned above. For guarding the <span class="h">Bris</span> is merited through the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> through <span class="h">Targum</span>, as explained well in the teaching mentioned above — see there. And then certainly he was no longer afraid of Esav who is the all-encompassing evil, for he falls automatically, in the aspect of <span class="mx">"tongue falls upon tongue"</span> [<span class="h">lashon nofel al lashon</span>], as explained there — see there. Therefore the first words of Yaakov that he sent to Esav were: <span class="v">"I dwelt with Lavan"</span> — with Lavan specifically, who is <span class="h">Lashon Targum</span>. He subdued the evil from there and clarified the good. And then Esav falls automatically as mentioned above. And this is: <span class="v">"and I had an ox and a donkey, flocks"</span> etc. — meaning the good sparks and wealth that he clarified from there. Therefore Esav went to Yishma'el, for everything goes to its kind — meaning, as the teaching states, Esav and Yishma'el are the generality of the seventy nations. Therefore he went there so that the evil of the generality of the seventy nations would combine together, to overpower Yaakov, G-d forbid. But Yaakov, through having subdued Lavan, was overpowering them, as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore Yaakov specifically established <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span>, for <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span> is the aspect of <span class="h">Targum</span> — for the essential perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> is through this, as mentioned above. And this was the aspect of Yaakov's tikunim as mentioned above. Therefore <span class="h">Arvis</span> is hinted at in the large <span class="h">ayin</span> of <span class="v">"Shma"</span> — which is the <span class="h">roshei teivos</span> [initial letters] of <span class="h">Shacharis Minchah Arvis</span>, as the holy Zohar states. For <span class="h">Arvis</span> is in the aspect of <span class="h">Targum</span>, in the aspect of the Tree of Knowledge — from where one merits to subdue the seventy nations and to merit the aspect of the seventy souls of the house of Yaakov as mentioned above. And it corresponds to <span class="h">Sukkos</span>, which is the aspect of Yaakov, for on <span class="h">Sukkos</span> one subdues the seventy nations that diminish and go — corresponding to the diminishing bulls of the festival.</div>

<div class="p">And this is the aspect of <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis Reshus</span>. For <span class="h">Targum</span> is the aspect of <span class="h">reshus</span> [the permitted], the aspect of the permissible, which is in the aspect of the Tree of Knowledge — <span class="h">Nogah</span>, the aspect of <span class="h">Targum</span>, as is known. For the obligation of a <span class="h">mitzvah</span> and the forbidden are in the aspect of holiness and its opposite. But the permitted and <span class="h">reshus</span> [optional/mundane] is in the aspect of <span class="h">Targum</span>, the Tree of Knowledge, as is known. Therefore <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span> is <span class="h">reshus</span> as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">And this is the aspect of <span class="h">chatzos</span> [midnight]. For the night is divided into two, because it is in the aspect of the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil. Therefore it is divided into two: for the first half of the night is the time of the hold of the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>, as is known. But we perform <span class="h">mitzvos</span> and tikunim also in the first half of the night — meaning <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span> and <span class="h">Krias Shma</span>, and <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> upon the bed. And then we subdue the evil and clarify the good, and then we merit <span class="h">chatzos</span> — meaning to divide the night so that the second half of the night transforms to complete good and is subsumed in day: <span class="v">"night will shine like day"</span> (Tehilim 139). For from midnight onward the aspect of <span class="h">chesed</span>, which is the light of day, is revealed. Therefore Dovid HaMelech, peace upon him, was careful with <span class="h">chatzos</span>, for this is the perfection of <span class="h">Malchus</span>, which is the aspect of the perfection of <span class="h">Lashon HaKodesh</span> through <span class="h">Targum</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="h">chatzos</span> as mentioned above. Therefore the time of marital union is after midnight, for then the aspect of Chavah-Woman is built through the tikun of the Tree of Knowledge — which is the aspect of deep slumber and sleep, made through <span class="h">chatzos</span>, which is the breaking of sleep, the breaking of night, the aspect of breaking the Tree of Knowledge — and then it is subsumed in good: <span class="v">"night will shine like day."</span> Therefore from midnight the aspect of <span class="h">chesed</span>, the light of day, is revealed, as mentioned above.</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!--                     HALACHAH 3 (on LM I:52)                  -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->

<div class="ts">
<div class="sn">Halachah 3</div>
<div class="ssn">The matter of Tefilas Arvis Reshus [the evening prayer being optional]</div>
</div>

<div class="p">Based on the teaching: <span class="v">"One who is awake at night"</span> etc., <span class="v">"his soul is liable"</span> — in <span class="lr">LM I:52</span>, see there very, very well.</div>

<div class="p">For there are heretics who say that the world is a necessary reality [<span class="h">mechuyav ha'metzius</span>], G-d forbid. But in truth the world is a possible reality [<span class="h">efshari ha'metzius</span>]. Only after the souls of Israel were emanated, Hashem was, as it were, compelled to create the world and everything in it for the sake of Israel. For everything was created for our sake. It emerges that now, when the souls of Israel are found in the world, certainly the world is a necessary reality. And from this comes their error and heresy as mentioned above. But in truth, before the souls of Israel were emanated, the world was a possible reality. Only immediately upon the emanation of the souls of Israel, Hashem immediately needed to create the world for their sake, as mentioned above. Therefore after the souls of Israel were created, the world is in the aspect of a necessary reality. And through Israel doing His will and being included in Him — for which purpose the entire world was created — through this the entire world together with the souls of Israel is included in Hashem, Who is a necessary reality; and then the entire world becomes a necessary reality. And this is: <span class="v">"one who is awake at night"</span> etc., <span class="v">"his soul is liable"</span> [<span class="h">mischayyev b'nafsho</span> — also readable as: makes himself necessary through his soul]. See there well.</div>

<div class="p">And this is the aspect of <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis Reshus</span>. For Yaakov established <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span>. For prayer is the aspect of the renewal of the world, as is explained and understood in the words of Rabbainu of blessed memory in several places. For prayer is His oneness — in the aspect of <span class="v">"He is your praise and He is your G-d."</span> And the speech of prayer is the aspect of the Word of Hashem through which heaven and earth were made, in the aspect of <span class="v">"through the Word of Hashem the heavens were made,"</span> as explained in the words of Rabbainu of blessed memory elsewhere. And this is the aspect of <span class="v">"Ad-nai, open my lips"</span> that we say before the prayer, for the speech of prayer is the Word of Hashem as mentioned above. It emerges that prayer is the aspect of the renewal of the world, the aspect of the Word of Hashem etc. as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span> is <span class="h">reshus</span>. For the revelation of creation is the aspect of light — the aspect of <span class="v">"G-d said: let there be light"</span> etc. And before creation, this is the aspect of darkness. For before creation it is impossible to comprehend, and therefore it is called the aspect of darkness — too deep for comprehension. In the aspect of <span class="v">"He forms light and creates darkness."</span> As is brought in the Kavanos [of the Ari"zal]: that <span class="h">Yetzirah</span> is called light and <span class="h">Beriyah</span> is called darkness, because <span class="h">Beriyah</span> is higher than <span class="h">Yetzirah</span> and it is impossible to comprehend there — therefore it is called darkness, too deep for comprehension. In the aspect of: <span class="v">"He placed darkness as His concealment."</span> Therefore also at the time of creation, Hashem created darkness before light — <span class="mx">"first darkness and then light."</span> For the darkness that preceded the light hints at before creation, which is the aspect of <span class="v">"He placed darkness as His concealment."</span> And then, in the aspect of darkness, in the aspect of before creation — meaning before the souls of Israel were emanated — the world was in the aspect of a possible reality, since the souls of Israel had not yet been created, as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">And this is the aspect of <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis Reshus</span>. For prayer is the aspect of the creation of the world. For prayer has a root above — for Hashem Himself also prays, as our Sages of blessed memory said: <span class="mx">"from where do we know that the Holy One blessed be He prays?"</span> etc. And at <span class="h">Arvis</span>, the prayer is in the aspect of <span class="h">reshus</span>, the aspect of a possible reality — for there is not yet an obligation, G-d forbid, to create the world, since the souls of Israel have also not yet been created. Therefore Yaakov established <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span>. For <span class="mx">"Israel arose in thought first,"</span> as it is written: <span class="v">"Bereishis [In the beginning] He created"</span> etc. — <span class="mx">"for the sake of Israel who are called 'raishis [first].'"</span> It emerges that the first thought of creation was Israel, and then, in the aspect of the first thought, the world was a possible reality as mentioned above — since the souls of Israel had not yet been created, only it arose in thought, and the matter was in His will. Therefore then, at the beginning of creation — meaning when Israel arose in thought first — the world was a possible reality as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore Yaakov established <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span>, which is <span class="h">reshus</span>. For the first thought is impossible to comprehend, and it is the aspect of darkness — too deep for comprehension, as mentioned above — and there the world is still in the aspect of a possible reality. Therefore there the prayer is in the aspect of <span class="h">reshus</span>. For, as it were, there is not yet an obligation to speak the words of prayer — which are the aspect of <span class="v">"through the Word of Hashem the heavens were made"</span> etc. as mentioned above. For the world is still a possible reality, in the aspect of <span class="h">reshus</span>, since Israel has not yet been created — only arose in thought, as mentioned above. Therefore at the time when the aspect of Yaakov begins to be revealed, the prayer is <span class="h">reshus</span> — the aspect of <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis Reshus</span> etc. as mentioned above. But afterward, when Yaakov established <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span> and the souls of Israel were revealed — for at night the souls of Israel are created, in the aspect of <span class="v">"new every morning"</span> etc. — therefore in the morning light, when the light of creation is revealed (for the essence of creation is the aspect of light as mentioned above), then the prayer is in the aspect of an obligation. For then, when the souls of Israel have already been revealed, Hashem was, as it were, obligated to speak and create the world for the sake of Israel, as mentioned above. Therefore then, by day — which is the essence of creation — after the souls of Israel have already emerged, the prayer, which is the Word of Hashem, is in the aspect of an obligation. For, as it were, Hashem is obligated to speak the aspect of prayer — which is the aspect of the Word of Hashem — and to create the world for the sake of Israel, since everything was created for the sake of Israel as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore the [other] nations — that is, Yishma'el and Esav — have a hold only on Avraham and Yitzchak. For the essence of their hold is from heresy, as is known. For their hold is from the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>, which is called <span class="mx">"a foreign god — heresy."</span> And the essence of the heresy is the heretical doctrine mentioned above: that they invert the words of the Living G-d and say that the world is, G-d forbid, a necessary reality. And this error flows down and chains down to them because in truth the world is a necessary reality after Israel was created, as mentioned above. It emerges that the essence of their hold is from the aspect of after creation — after the souls of Israel were created, when the world became, through the souls of Israel, the aspect of a necessary reality. And from this, a hold chains down to them for their heretical doctrine and foolishness as mentioned above. But at the root of the souls of Israel above, at their source, they have no hold at all. For there the world is still a possible reality and they have no hold there whatsoever.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore in Yaakov they have no hold at all, for <span class="mx">"Israel arose in thought first."</span> For even the essential holiness of Avraham and Yitzchak is only the aspect of Israel, which includes all three <span class="h">Avos</span>. And there is the essential general holiness of the three <span class="h">Avos</span>, as it is written: <span class="v">"for in Yitzchak shall seed be called to you"</span> etc. — <span class="mx">"and not all of Yitzchak"</span> etc. — for the essential thing is Israel, which arose in thought first. And this is the aspect of: <span class="v">"and I shall remember My covenant with Yaakov"</span> — and afterward: <span class="v">"and also My covenant with Yitzchak"</span> etc. It emerges that the first thought was Israel, and then the world was a possible reality — the aspect of <span class="h">Tefilas Arvis Reshus</span>, which is the prayer of Yaakov — and there they do not yet have any hold as mentioned above. But immediately upon Israel arising in thought and the souls of Israel beginning to be revealed, the world immediately becomes the aspect of a necessary reality. And then, when Avraham and Yitzchak were created — all of whom were created only for the sake of Israel, as it is written: <span class="v">"so says Hashem to the house of Yaakov, who redeemed Avraham"</span> — as our Sages of blessed memory said in the Midrash — then the world is the aspect of a necessary reality as mentioned above, since the aspect of the souls of Israel has already been revealed as mentioned above. Therefore then, by day — which is the essence of creation — the prayer is an obligation as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">And this is the aspect of <span class="v">"b'hibar'am — b'Avraham"</span> [when they were created — through Avraham]. For <span class="v">"Bereishis — He created"</span>: for the sake of Israel who are called <span class="h">raishis</span>, who arose in thought first — then He created. This is the aspect of a possible reality. But afterward, when Israel had already arisen in thought and the souls of Israel were emanated, then it is said: <span class="v">"these are the chronicles of heaven and earth when they were created [<i>b'hibar'am</i>]"</span> — <span class="v">"b'hibar'am"</span> specifically. This is the aspect of a necessary reality, for afterward the world becomes the aspect of a necessary reality for the sake of Israel. And then, by day — which is the prayer of Avraham and Yitzchak who emerged after Yaakov, for <span class="mx">"Israel arose in thought first"</span>; as it is written: <span class="v">"so says Hashem, your Creator, Yaakov"</span> etc.; <span class="mx">"My world, My world — who created you? Israel"</span> — therefore then, by day, when the souls of Israel have already been revealed, the prayer is in the aspect of an obligation as mentioned above. Therefore there, the nations have a hold, for the essence of their hold is from there as mentioned above. For in truth, the essential perfection of prayer is by day specifically. For in truth this is the essential perfection: when the world is in the aspect of a necessary reality — meaning when Hashem does the will of Israel and creates and sustains the entire world for their sake, as if He were obligated in the matter. This is the aspect of the world becoming a necessary reality for the sake of Israel, as mentioned above. And certainly this is the essential perfection, and the essential intention of creation was for this purpose: so that the world would be included afterward in the necessary reality through Israel, as mentioned above — in the teaching mentioned above, see there. But nevertheless, now they have a hold from this aspect specifically — from the aspect of after creation, meaning after the world was created for the sake of the souls of Israel that were emanated first. And then, after the souls of Israel were emanated, the world is the aspect of a necessary reality as mentioned above. And from there, a hold chains down to them for their heretical doctrine and foolishness as mentioned above. For Hashem gives them room to err, so that there should be free will in the world. But in the aspect of Yaakov — <span class="mx">"Israel that arose in thought first"</span> — there they have no hold whatsoever. For in truth, when the souls of Israel were emanated in thought first, the world was a possible reality, and in His good will He emanated the souls of Israel and afterward created the world for their sake etc. — as mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">Baruch Hashem l'olam, Amain v'Amain.</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">Hashem HaTov yechaper. Hashem HaTov yechaper.</span> For these words are very well-founded for one who understands them correctly, in truth and in faith.</div>

